ABSTRACTS={'A1-exact-benchmarks': 'We realize the generalized-baker benchmark as an ordinary physical piecewise-exact symplectic impact system and keep its coupled symbolic natural extension as a coding object rather than a fictitious symplectic inverse limit.  A global affine work coordinate produces the additive current, while a refinement-independent graded flag-current complex gives typed all-depth parameter response.  No bilateral Koopman gap or symbolic Hamiltonian leaf is used.', 'A2-sinai-homological-pressure': 'For the compact finite-horizon Lorentz family we construct a parent-branch moving transfer bundle, prove covariance damping at genuinely small frequencies, derive the lattice obstruction from returned-branch temporal nonintegrability and closing, and cover the complete Fourier line by an integrable moderate/very-high-frequency decomposition.  The resulting vector--collision-count--roof density theorem yields all local, central and saturated window regimes.', 'A3-full-empirical-path-ldp': 'The inducing process is treated as a graph-completed Markov-renewal process stopped at deterministic collision or physical time.  The state retains singularity exposure, completed profiles, the next excursion and its pointed terminal prefix.  An exact entropy-control representation gives one fixed good recurrent--recession rate and separate deterministic-clock contractions, without deleting finite-rate singular excursions or using a random speed.', 'A4-history-memory-universal-pressure': 'We prove weighted Wasserstein contraction for the actual complete-past kernel, derive the correctly centered Poisson martingale and a quenched enhanced suspension limit, construct the eigenfunction Doob nonlinear history semigroup, and obtain a normalized instantaneous--resonant--descriptor--decaying memory decomposition from a renewal resolvent with integrable vertical derivatives and all zero multiplicities retained.', 'B1-microcanonical-preparation': 'Microcanonical preparation is proved after exact particle-number coefficient extraction.  A canonical trajectory-polymer expansion supplies the full number/continuous Hessian, a compact-frequency gap and a speed-dependent integrable high-frequency estimate for the coefficient law.  A degree-one finite saddle and a relative local theorem for regular CLT-wide shells yield the source-dependent constrained pressure and covariance Schur complement.', 'B2-collision-clusters-dynamic-ldp': 'We construct the compatible Green trace graph and a direct fixed-horizon all-contact trajectory expansion for deterministic hard spheres.  Every fixed cyclic genealogy is treated with the full physical Jacobi map and genealogy-dependent sublevel constants, then removed by dominated summation against an explicit factorial majorant.  Exact time composition, bounded-source exhaustion and smooth positive controlled recoveries yield the grand-canonical and microcanonical density--actual-contact LDPs.', 'B3-hamilton-boltzmann-cotangents': 'On a perturbative Maxwellian phase chart we prove a nonautonomous kinetic energy estimate and construct the joint density--contact Gaussian field directly from microscopic marked cumulants.  The collision noise acts on the exact dual coefficient $\\Delta p+\\psi$, including direct contact variance.  The covariance kernel, Cameron--Martin domain, second epi-derivative and stopping-time process tightness are then identified without omitting the contact coordinate.', 'B4-nonlinear-kinetic-semigroups': 'Microscopic states, Koopman observables, pushed-forward laws, endpoint log-Laplace values and the limiting Nisio semigroup are kept distinct.  A resolvent image of smooth reflected observables gives the graph core, and the hierarchy corrector converges in an exponential-generating sequence space.  Compact dynamic-action sublevels and nonlinear-resolvent comparison identify the kinetic semigroup without uncontrolled doubled viscosity jets or repeated preparation cost.', 'C1-information-risk-sensitive-saddles': 'The exact information state is a positive posterior law obtained by integrated coarea/Rokhlin disintegration; oriented currents retain only geometry.  A compact evidence-direction cone closes the zero-evidence boundary, and the full-belief controlled kernel satisfies a Feller DPP.  A growing moment coordinate has a quantitative Wasserstein error, while coefficient-first inserted local limits yield controlled LAN and Bernstein--von Mises only on uniformly informative regular strategies.', 'C2-cotangent-rigidity-tangent-representations': 'The weighted cotangent dual is the vector space of invariant signed Radon measures, with probabilities as its positive normalized slice.  Equality of the full perturbed pressure functional is treated platform by platform, never inferred from one scalar value.  Spectral response and physical memory are placed on separately constructed common-domain bundles, and source perturbations, state tangents, optional projections and quadratic BSDE limits are rigorously typed.', 'D1-deterministic-theta-contractions': 'We construct genuine positive microscopic phase labels from separated components of an already proved platform rate, retain an explicit boundary band, and use the same label at every observable projection.  Restricted and conditional component laws, normalized component pressures, phase-local coefficients and exact positive mixture contraction yield the nonconvex physical rate without Riesz projections as probabilities or double counting phase costs.'}
